<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

	<!--
		The papillon's cocoon (archive/CASTES-PLAN.md §7). A greenworm who has spent enough mana spins it,
		sits inside it for fifteen days, and comes out a papillon - see
		Source/Insects/PapillonMaturation.cs for the whole chain and the four decisions behind it.

		Why a building and not a hediff: a hediff cannot render anything on its own, and it cannot hold
		a pawn either. The sac is the holder - its comp keeps her in a container of its own, the way a
		cryptosleep casket or a biosculpter pod does - so she is off the map for the fifteen days and
		the tile shows a sac and nothing else.

		`PassThroughOnly` is what keeps a sac in a corridor from being a wall, and it is also what makes
		the cell under it free the moment it opens. That and the art are the abaddon's egg sac's own,
		which is deliberate: the sac is what a player already associates with a brood turning into
		something else.

		The sac's own rule is that only a `KillFinalize` counts (see Things_EggSpew.xml). This one is
		the opposite, on purpose: the comp kills the woman inside it when the cocoon is broken at
		all, except for the `Vanish` mode it uses to remove itself on hatching. That was the user's
		ruling, 2026-10-02: she dies with her cocoon.
	-->
	<ThingDef ParentName="BuildingNaturalBase">
		<defName>PMM_Cocoon</defName>
		<label>papillon cocoon</label>
		<description>A papery cocoon spun by a greenworm, with something moving faintly inside it. Break it before its time and whatever is in there dies with it.</description>
		<thingClass>Building</thingClass>
		<category>Building</category>
		<!-- A building is not ticked unless it says so, and the comp inside this one is what opens it:
		     with no ticker type nothing inside it ever ran, so the sac held her forever and an empty one
		     never cleared itself either. A def's ticker type has to match the override its comp writes:
		     `CompTickRare` is ours and wants `Rare`, one pass every 250 ticks - about four seconds - which
		     is nothing against a fifteen-day wait. The cryptosleep casket in Core sets `Normal` for its own
		     reasons; the two defs disagree because their comps differ, not because either is wrong. -->
		<tickerType>Rare</tickerType>
		<graphicData>
			<texPath>Things/Building/PMM_EggSac</texPath>
			<graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
		</graphicData>
		<altitudeLayer>Building</altitudeLayer>
		<passability>PassThroughOnly</passability>
		<fillPercent>0.3</fillPercent>
		<rotatable>false</rotatable>
		<terrainAffordanceNeeded>Light</terrainAffordanceNeeded>
		<!-- Paper and silk, and the same 0.4 the egg sac sets. With no value at all the def inherits
		     none, so fire could not touch the sac - which would make the comp's own promise that a raid
		     or a fire kills her a promise the def breaks. -->
		<Flammability>0.4</Flammability>
		<!-- What a collapsed sac leaves behind. The parent's rock rubble is what a stone wall leaves,
		     not what paper does. -->
		<filthLeaving>Filth_Dirt</filthLeaving>
		<statBases>
			<!-- Four times the egg sac's 20, and it is the wait rather than the material: a cocoon is
			     paper and silk, and fifteen days is a long time to ask a raid to leave something alone. -->
			<MaxHitPoints>80</MaxHitPoints>
			<WorkToBuild>0</WorkToBuild>
		</statBases>
		<comps>
			<li Class="PMM_Insects.CompProperties_PapillonCocoon" />
		</comps>
	</ThingDef>

</Defs>
